RT-10: give the keyboard back to the console when the server ends
(build-tree patch, applied after rt08-banded-default.patch; built as s14rt04).

rtgOpenInput makes the server's screen the screen manager's active one
(SIOCACTIVATE, without displaying it).  When that screen closes, the kernel
(console/screen.c CloseScreen) looks for a successor only in the screen's
own group -- ours has none -- and then sets activescreen to 0, and a key
arriving with no active screen is dropped.  After every RTG X session the
console therefore took no typing (A4000T MG11; rig: s8rt04 and s13rt04
both).  rtgCloseScreen and rtgAbort now issue SIOCBACK (HideScreen) on the
screen before it goes away: it acts only while ours is still the active
screen and selects the first usable other one, the console.  Rig, one
boot: console typing works after s14rt04 three times and after a lost
keyboard from s8/s13 (a later s14 session recovers it).  A kill -9 of the
server still loses it: SIGKILL runs no server code.

--- a/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/rtgInit.c
+++ b/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/rtgInit.c
@@ -140,11 +140,35 @@
     rtgMonitorSwitch(SVGAMONITORSWITCH_SVGA);
 }
 
+/*
+** Give the keyboard back to the console (RT-10).  rtgOpenInput made our
+** screen the screen manager's active one (SIOCACTIVATE) without displaying
+** it; closing it leaves the kernel with no active screen at all -- its
+** CloseScreen looks for a successor only in our (empty) screen group and
+** then clears activescreen, and a key with no active screen is dropped
+** (console screen.c) -- so after X the console took no typing (A4000T,
+** MG11).  SIOCBACK (HideScreen) acts only while our screen is still the
+** active one and selects the first usable other screen, the console; a
+** user who switched screens meanwhile is left alone.
+*/
+static void
+rtgInputBack(fd)
+int fd;
+{
+    if (fd >= 0 && ioctl(fd, SIOCBACK, 0))
+        ErrorF("rtgInputBack: SIOCBACK failed (%s)\n", strerror(errno));
+}
+
 /* Fatal error or GiveUp (AbortDDX, amixIo.c): back to the Amiga video. */
 void
 rtgAbort()
 {
+    int i;
+
     rtgMonitorSwitch(SVGAMONITORSWITCH_Amiga);
+    for (i = 0; i < MAXSCREENS; i++)    /* no CloseScreen on this path */
+        if (amixFbs[i].mapped)
+            rtgInputBack(amixFbs[i].fd);
 }
 
 static Bool
@@ -170,6 +194,7 @@
 
     if (amixFbs[i].mapped && amixFbs[i].fd >= 0)
     {
+        rtgInputBack(amixFbs[i].fd);
         if (CloseScreen(amixFbs[i].fd))
             ErrorF("rtgCloseScreen: CloseScreen(%d) failed\n", amixFbs[i].fd);
         amixFbs[i].fd     = -1;
